1
00:00:00,079 --> 00:00:01,560
For years, I watched creators play

2
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,439
the craziest Minecraft challenges.

3
00:00:03,439 --> 00:00:04,679
The floor is lava.

4
00:00:04,679 --> 00:00:06,440
Every block drops something random.

5
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:07,960
One heart for the whole game.

6
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,779
And every time, I thought: why can't

7
00:00:09,779 --> 00:00:11,009
I just play this myself?

8
00:00:11,315 --> 00:00:12,655
So in April twenty twenty-five,

9
00:00:12,655 --> 00:00:13,635
I wrote the first few challenges

10
00:00:13,635 --> 00:00:15,635
into a mod. Then came more.

11
00:00:15,635 --> 00:00:17,135
A timer, a challenge picker,

12
00:00:17,135 --> 00:00:18,035
a level tree with XP,

13
00:00:18,035 --> 00:00:19,975
until there were fifty of them.

14
00:00:19,975 --> 00:00:21,095
Then I went further.

15
00:00:21,095 --> 00:00:21,515
A whole casino,

16
00:00:21,515 --> 00:00:23,435
where the House always wins.

17
00:00:23,435 --> 00:00:25,175
And now I'm teaching an AI called Bob

18
00:00:25,175 --> 00:00:27,285
to play Lockout Bingo against you.

19
00:00:27,452 --> 00:00:28,572
It's called Challenge Craft,

20
00:00:28,572 --> 00:00:29,792
it's free on CurseForge,

21
00:00:29,792 --> 00:00:31,482
and this is only the beginning.

